WEBVTT

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.030
Play!

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:46.370
Izumi!

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:47.670
What's with that?

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.500
Nishiura is rather lively.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.340
Their third round was right before summer vacation, after all.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.550
But honestly, this coach really messes with the batting order.

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:01.260
That's because their fourth batter, Tajima, was injured, right?

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.930
That's right.

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.350
Tajima Yuuichirou is with them.

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.310
I really wanted Tajima.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:10.480
I wanted him to come to our school and be the core of our first years.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:13.570
Trying to scout him was a total misfire.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:16.440
No matter how much we talked, we couldn't catch his interest.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.860
Well, you know, that's probably my fault.

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:21.490
Strike!

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:24.410
But if we can achieve our goal at this tournament,

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.910
I feel like our luck will change next year.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.210
Goal? You mean best eight?

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.000
I'm looking at reality.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.750
A bunt after two outs?

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.260
Safe! Safe!

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.880
He's fast! About five seconds?

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.050
Who is that?

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:43.350
Bijou's coach?

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.390
He's good, but he's still on the mend.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:50.270
He's playing at third base again, so I don't think that's it.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.150
I see.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.860
But really, how lax of Kounan.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.690
Tajima bunted four times in the previous game.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:58.780
Why isn't the third baseman on the lookout?

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.490
The first run!

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:02.870
Here we go!

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.080
It's cold!

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.450
Strike!

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.290
So the only one we need to be wary of is Tajima?

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:10.620
On the offensive front.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.130
You're talking about the pitcher's quirky throw?

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.210
It's that Mihashi guy, right?

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.130
Yeah.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.220
Second!

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:24.510
They're playing catch?

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.640
Watch carefully.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.970
They managed to hold Tousei down to four runs with that pitch.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:33.190
That's not it! What Tamaken was talking about back then was...

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.310
Makoto!

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:35.110
Yes, sir!

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.980
Stop messing around and quiet down the first years!

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:37.690
Yes, sir!

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:41.400
Second and third years, too. Don't get excited just because you won a game!

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.450
Yes, sir!

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:43.780
Look, you guys better watch carefully.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:44.910
We'll be playing them next.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:47.410
You say the heart is their catcher?

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.040
Just watch.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:50.700
Ball.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:53.870
Strike!

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.380
What a weird lead.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.670
They're all breaking balls.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:04:01.170
The fastball is their finisher, so it seems like they save it until the end of the game.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.880
So that's the quirky pitch? What else...

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:06.970
It looks like he has good control.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:07.720
Out!

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.640
He's 100 for 100.
Nice, shortstop.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:10.720
You're exaggerating.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.310
It's not an exaggeration.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.980
Even if that were true, what about it?

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:18.520
I watched two games, but that pitcher didn't shake his head even once.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:19.230
He'd give away the pitch type if he did that, right?

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:20.360
Nice pitch!

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.280
Good pitching!

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.820
The catcher will change signs until he nods.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:25.410
Strike!

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.530
That's not it.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:31.580
It seems like he's really throwing
exactly as the catcher tells him to.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:35.080
Strike!

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.790
In other words,

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.710
we should aim for that slow breaking ball.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:43.300
If the pitcher won't intervene with the pitch order, then we just need to read the catcher.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:43.760
Strike!

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:44.630
With only one person, there's bound to be a pattern.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.180
Nice pitch!

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.050
Two outs!

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:50.560
The fact that he has good control is just another lucky break for us.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.640
How many games do we have data on?

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:53.930
Including today, three games.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:54.890
That's plenty.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:57.230
Here we come, best eight.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:01.650
Winner: Nishiura High School.
Please commence ground maintenance.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:04.190
Time to exchange cheers!

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.910
We'll start with "Hurray! Hurray! Nishiura!"

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:10.530
And then "Hurray! Hurray! Kounan!"

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:11.620
Yeah!

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:14.000
Hurray~! Hurray~!

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.620
It's Hamada's cheers.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:16.920
We won toda—

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.080
We won today too.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.000
What?

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.290
We thought the same thing.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:21.710
Next, the left side.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:24.510
We were able to win because of Abe, too...

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:28.340
Um, hey... Abe, you...

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:31.140
About Nishiura... W-Won't qui—

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:34.310
There's no way I'd quit!
What's with you asking that lately!?

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:35.890
I-If you won't quit, then that's good!

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:39.190
Do you want me to quit!? Or not!?

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.150
Stop playing around and stretch!

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:47.150
I-If you quit, then I wouldn't be able to pitch anymore.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:49.110
Is that what this is about?

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:52.160
You really worry about one thing after another.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.000
I'll say it as many times as you need.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.370
I'm going to be catcher for all three years!

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.500
If I say I'll do it, I will! Got it?

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.790
Y-Yeah!

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.960
If you're not going to stretch, then help out with the maintenance!

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.800
Yes? This is Hanai.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.310
Okay. Okay, I understand.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:18.440
They can't move the car, so we're going to carry the luggage to the parking lot.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:19.980
Okay.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.860
It's the pool's parking lot, right?

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.020
The far one?

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:24.400
If we go around back, it'll be just around the corner.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.320
Towards the pool.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:27.780
Don't you carry anything.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.160
A-Are you okay!?

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.780
Here, I'll take it.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.580
You're too jumpy.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:37.830
It'll all end if you jam a single finger on your right hand.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.250
Watch over the luggage.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:42.210
Hey, hey! The bats were in the most danger right then, weren't they?

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.960
If they got cracked, they'd be useless.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:47.050
In the worst case, you could buy new bats.

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:50.130
What!? That's some weird logic.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:51.760
I'm sure Mihashi thinks so too.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:55.350
Sorry about that. I mean, the guy isn't very conscious of himself.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.440
If I'm on luggage duty, I won't get injured.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:05.520
Hey, Mihashi! Hello, I'm Abe's dad.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:07.440
It seemed like you were in good form today too, huh?

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:08.440
Nice pitching!

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:12.200
What are you doing on your own? Luggage duty?

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:14.200
How is Takaya?

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.410
He's noisy, isn't he?

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:20.160
Huh? Could it be that you find me scary?

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:23.500
Come on. Don't shrink away!

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.670
Acting like a timid person!

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:28.510
You're always arguing with Takaya, right?

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.260
It's Mihashi without a doubt.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:40.480
Aren't you scared of Takaya, Mihashi?

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:42.940
Takaya? Does he mean Abe?

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:46.360
I am.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:51.610
Yes?

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:55.990
Is that right? I'll go right away.
Where are you now?

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:58.620
Okay.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:01.120
Well then, Mihashi, good luck in the next game too!

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:07.880
That person is Abe's... father.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:09.920
88.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:11.170
89.

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:12.470
90.

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:15.430
91.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:17.970
92.

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:22.810
Last one. 100!

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.440
Good work!

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:30.230
Takeshi. The meeting for the fifth game is starting.

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:31.610
Seriously!? What time is it?

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:32.740
Ah, this is bad!

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:34.700
Hey!

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:37.280
Kiyo, put away the balls and equipment.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:38.450
Yes, of course.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:39.450
Sorry about this.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:40.910
Not at all.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:43.330
He found out about the extra training.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:48.040
There probably won't be a fight or anything, but things get tense when those two talk.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.630
Don't you think you're doing a little too much after having a game today?

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.380
Your knees are worn out.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:57.050
But it's something I always do.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:00.560
It's more worrisome that you're able to put on that mask while your legs are so shaky.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.020
I guess that's true.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:06.770
Well, when I see that side of you,
I do think it's why you got chosen.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:07.560
Here.

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:09.270
Thank you.

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:12.650
Even now, I'm getting called to the meeting like this.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:16.070
If there's an opening, I'll still aim to be catcher.

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.240
Yeah.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:23.040
But just like how you accept me as right fielder, I also accept you as the official catcher.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.830
If the catcher is uneasy, then everyone will become uneasy, right?

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.000
Have some confidence.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.420
I understand.

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:31.540
Work hard.

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:32.880
Yeah.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:35.970
Naomasa is a good guy.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:41.350
Although he thinks he's stronger,
he's still considerate of me.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:44.970
If you can do as I say, then I'll push you forward.

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:48.770
It's because you're a good guy that the coach picked me.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:50.770
I'll do anything.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:53.190
It's for that reason that I was able to become a regular.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:56.150
Excuse me. I've brought Takeshi.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:59.200
We're all here, then. Let's get started.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.780
If we beat Nishiura, we'll be in the best eight.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:06.540
That's not true.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.870
I mean, I've been going to every game!

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:14.340
But in middle school, I asked three times and he told me not to come every time, didn't he?

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:16.590
That happened?

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.470
I said so at the time.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:20.930
You always forget things right away.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:25.850
Are you sure he wasn't just embarrassed
because he wasn't able to stand out at Mihoshi?

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:28.180
You really think that's what it was?

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:30.730
I'm home.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:33.310
Ren, welcome home!

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:34.650
D-Dad!

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:37.440
Dad! It's been a long time!

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:40.660
Ren, you won again today? That's awesome!

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:42.450
There's grilled bean-jam buns.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.080
Bean-jam buns!

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.950
How many safe hits were you able to make?

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:47.790
Five!

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:50.290
That's good! So they scored one run?

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.920
Ah, no, two?

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:52.880
Three!

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:56.170
Well, sometimes that happens, right?

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:57.840
The opponent must have been strong too.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:00.380
Mom! Grill them! Grill them!

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:02.300
Dinner's about ready.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:03.090
Later, okay?

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:05.100
Grill them now!

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:07.890
Well then, why don't we practice a bit?

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:10.100
It's been a long time since I caught your pitches, Ren.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.390
I can't.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:16.690
I pitched in a game today, so I can't throw anymore.

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:17.900
Here it comes.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.190
Don't you pitch all day?

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:23.490
I don't. Because...

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:27.120
What's with that? That's kind of gross, Ren.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:31.290
Ren, the next game is the day after tomorrow, right?

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:31.960
Yeah.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:36.420
I have a day off on that day, you know.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:38.550
Then, will you come to see Hamada?

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:39.710
H-Hamada?

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:41.720
Wait, who's that?

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.300
I told you before.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:46.350
The kid of the Hamadas next door at the Yamagishi Villa.

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:49.060
You said something about him being in the same class?

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:50.270
That's right.

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:52.940
Ren, here. I'll grill one skewer for you.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:56.400
I just remembered. What an amazing bond.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:01.900
When Ren was pitcher at the farewell party, he got his glove from Hamada.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:04.860
Back then, we couldn't buy you one...

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:06.450
Wait! It's okay to go!?

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:08.620
Go wash your hands and bring down your laundry.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:09.910
Okay!

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:14.960
Five safe hits and three runs from line-drives.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:18.920
It's bad enough that they hit my pitches,
but I won't selfishly pitch as I please anymore.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:21.920
I'll listen to everything Abe says.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:28.220
It's bad for your digestion if you eat with such a disgruntled face.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.510
Yeah, it's delicious.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:32.930
You're not listening.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.770
And with this, it's three runs.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:38.480
What do you think about those three runs?

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:38.860
I think there was nothing we could
do about the second batter's long hit.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:41.440
Shun, stop playing games. It's 10 o'clock.

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:44.950
It's fine to include one or two of those kinds of hits in planning for a game.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:49.160
But I misread the timing of the third batter.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:53.910
That one hit raised Kounan's spirit while
agitating us and letting us make mistakes.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:54.210
Strike!

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:58.000
Did the pitcher agree to throwing those pitches that got hit?

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.920
It's got nothing to do with whether he agreed or not.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:03.010
He's just pitching as I tell him to.

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:06.010
What? What do you take the pitcher for?

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:08.260
That's not what I mean!

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:09.850
Mihashi is...

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.680
I mean, he trusts in me.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:19.190
Again, using such a fancy word as "trust."

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:21.520
I guess it'd be pitiful to poke fun at him.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:24.030
But...

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:27.200
Are you getting along with Mihashi?

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.610
Yeah, I am.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:32.240
You don't have any friends, do you?

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.910
Why are you saying that all of a sudden?

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:39.580
There's no need for me to become friends with the pitcher, right?

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:41.340
That's not it.

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:44.460
What I mean is that if you think you're getting along with Mihashi now,

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:48.050
then your friendships don't amount to much.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:49.970
You're wrong.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:54.180
I'd be able to communicate with
anyone other than Mihashi a lot better.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:58.140
It's not even funny how little my words got through in the beginning.

00:13:58.140 --> 00:13:59.900
Words, you say?

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:02.690
Hey, I'm really working hard here.

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.820
Somehow, Mihashi is really different,

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.820
and just continuing a conversation for ten minutes is really hard!

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:10.490
Are you sure it's not because of you?

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.330
It's not!

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:15.450
Don't pound the table! You'll spill the soy sauce!

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:18.870
Dad! Stop provoking Taka!

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.960
Taka, too. Once you're done eating, hurry and go to bed.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.290
You won't be able to get up tomorrow.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:25.250
Mom, can I have another cup?

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:27.260
I think I'm sobering up.

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:30.090
No way. You have to watch your blood sugar level.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:30.970
What!?

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.310
Even though he's never even talked with Mihashi before...

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:36.970
What does that old man think he knows!?

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:40.100
Well, I'm grateful that he's helped out on various things.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:41.440
Like today's video.

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:47.690
I have friends, don't I?

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:49.610
I mean, for the most part,
I'm friendly with everyone on the team.

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:51.950
Although we don't really go anywhere together.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.410
We've only known each other for three months, after all.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:57.410
If I were to go out somewhere, it'd be with seniors or kids from middle school...

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:58.950
Huh?

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:01.580
After getting into high school, they haven't contacted me even once...

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:03.330
And... they've never come?

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:05.340
I only ran into Haruna by chance?

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:10.260
That doesn't have anything
to do with Mihashi, though!

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:14.260
If you think you're getting along with Mihashi...

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:19.100
Even if you hadn't said anything,
I know that something is off right now.

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:23.480
But, even then, I'm trying my hardest!

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:28.320
8-0 against Sakitama, and 6-3 against Kounan.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:33.030
Even those at the office who said that the Tousei game was a fluke have approved an interview.

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:36.780
Newly established with ten first years.
Not to mention, the coach is a woman!

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:39.370
No matter the angle, I can come up with a header.

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:41.460
Anyone would get excited over this!

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:44.170
Good afternoon!

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:47.920
Looking from up close, the coach looks really young!

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.010
She's pretty. Looks strong.

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.380
Huge breasts!

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:56.550
I called from Saikyou Sports. I'm Shimizu.

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:59.350
This is my cameraman, Masaki.

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:04.310
I'm Momoe, the coach. Nice to meet you.

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:07.770
She's got a nice feel to her.

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:09.940
Please, come in.

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:12.320
Excuse us.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:16.700
I know it's sudden, but the grounds... are rather small, aren't they?

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:18.120
There's not enough space for the outfield.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:18.740
Yes.

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:22.370
Not to mention, to the left is the softball club.

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:23.080
Yes.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:27.170
And to the center and right are rugby poles, right?

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:28.380
Yes, that's right.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:31.800
They can only use the infield freely?

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.590
They take turns using it.

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:38.550
How tough. I can see their strong will to keep the bench clean while using it.

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:40.970
It also feels like they take care of their equipment.

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.520
But...

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:44.350
Nishihiro, last one!

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:45.310
Okay!

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:47.230
Back! Back!

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:48.900
Okay, nice catch!

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:49.980
What was left?

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:50.730
They're all energetic and I know they're a good team, but they're really normal.

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:51.900
The meeting.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:54.150
They're all energetic and I know they're a good team, but they're really normal.

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:56.950
I think it would be interesting if there were some sort of twist.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:58.620
An interview!?

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.330
Saikyou Sports?

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:02.700
Yeah, they were talking about it this morning.

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.290
It's a woman.

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.330
They'll talk to us too, right?

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:07.000
Yeah.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.080
Hey, Hamada.

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:13.710
About the interview... Try your best not to leak any information.

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:15.840
And be very courteous.

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:18.390
Oh, yeah. You're in the middle of a tournament, after all.

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:21.350
Sakaeguchi, we're going to eat.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:25.560
I want to set up tomorrow's meeting during the lunch break.

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.350
I've told the coach.

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:29.560
No problem. Have fun!

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:31.900
From five to nine o'clock?

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:35.280
You've really got a considerable amount of practice time.

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.370
You brought a lunch box today, right?

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:41.780
Y-Yeah.

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:43.660
Want to eat at one of the school cafeteria tables, then?

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:44.620
Cafeteria!

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:47.580
If we're going to the cafeteria,
I want to eat something.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:51.790
That's not right. We can get inside, but they're not serving.

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:53.460
Summer break is vacation time.

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:56.880
But it's possible that they're still serving.

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:58.970
I wonder if Abe knows?

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:02.720
Should I ask? It's fine if I don't ask, right?

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:05.600
It doesn't seem like he's thinking about much of anything.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:07.560
He's really slow at locking up too.

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:09.400
Got it.

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:10.520
Let's go!

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:17.400
Is there anything about me you're dissatisfied with?

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.320
How about in terms of my lead?

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:25.450
That's what I figured.

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:26.540
Then, it's fine.

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:31.830
Did I do something to seem discontent?

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:33.290
When? Where?

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:36.460
I have to be more careful.

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:40.180
If Abe hates me, it'll be over for me!

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:55.980
Haruka! Asuka!

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:57.820
Your big brother made the newspaper!

00:18:58.650 --> 00:18:59.320
Where?

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.450
No way!

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:02.870
Look! Look!

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:04.370
See?

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:06.490
Where?

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:15.840
To all guests: Smoking is prohibited in the stadium.

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:18.010
Hamada?

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:19.590
Long time no see!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:22.090
You got so big!

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:25.100
Mr. Mihashi, you really look like a proper member of society now.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:26.930
You used to have long hair, right?

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:30.140
Haruka and Asuka?

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:31.560
What do you say?

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:32.640
Good afternoon.

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:35.150
So cute!

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:37.820
Two girls!

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:40.070
I should have tried for another one!

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:40.990
Me too!

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:44.410
I was so scared it would be
another boy that I couldn't do it.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:47.660
You're all still young. Can't you still try for it?

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.660
What? It's impossible.

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:52.830
I heard that Mrs. Tajima
was 42 when she had Yuu.

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:53.500
What!?

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.170
How powerful!

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:57.040
Makes you respect her.

00:19:57.040 --> 00:19:58.800
It's Sakaeguchi's older sister!

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:00.880
Miss Sakaeguchi!

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:02.930
I thought it was you!

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:05.260
How've you been?

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:07.100
You came to cheer with your younger brother, I see.

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:08.390
It's been a long time.

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:13.850
Although our sons didn't talk much, both of their fathers are on the PTA.

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:14.650
Right?

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:15.770
Yes!

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:16.900
Is your father doing well?

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.900
Yes, he is! How about Mr. Abe?

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:20.320
He came today.

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:22.070
Mrs. Suyama's husband?

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:23.360
Nice to meet you.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:25.070
You're off work?

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.870
Just coasting through summer vacation.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:28.410
Where's your husband?

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:29.660
He's not coming.

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:31.830
He's got absolutely no interest in baseball!

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:36.120
As expected, the opponent's starting pitcher is Takenouchi.

00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:42.130
Just as we confirmed yesterday, how fast we can grasp his pitches will decide the game.

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:44.010
Let's start this with fighting spirit!

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:44.720
Yeah!

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:48.550
It's hot today too, so everyone be sure to watch your body's condition.

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:51.060
I won't forgive you if your legs cramp up from dehydration!

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:51.680
Yes!

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:54.850
Nishiura High School, please enter.

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:55.640
Yeah!

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:57.650
Well then, let's go!

00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:58.360
Yeah!

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:01.780
This feeling... Managed by the prefecture, huh?

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:05.070
Skipping prep school and coming here...

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:08.570
Did I want to see Nishiura lose?

00:21:08.570 --> 00:21:10.120
Last one!

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:12.080
Nice pitch!

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:14.290
Two more minutes for fielding practice.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:16.580
Are you feeling tired from two days ago?

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:18.170
I-I'm not.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:19.920
Okay. Your pitches are looking good, too.

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:21.460
The regulation went well this time.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:24.210
Listen up. The other side has three pitchers.

00:21:24.210 --> 00:21:26.470
Don't let them mess with your pace!

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:28.180
Because we only have you!

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:31.180
Yeah!

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:32.930
I won't crumble!

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:34.890
I'm in good condition today, too!

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:37.270
It feels good catching, too.

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:39.440
I-It's all thanks to Abe.

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:44.570
The ball count, stretching, rice balls...

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:46.780
If I were by myself, I couldn't...

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:48.280
It's all because of Abe!

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:50.780
Me being in good condition is all...

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:54.580
So I want to w-w-win!

00:21:58.170 --> 00:21:59.880
So you understand!

00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:01.540
I-I do!

00:22:02.290 --> 00:22:06.760
I can't really tell what this guy thinks about,
but I'm getting through to him!

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:09.970
I'm going to let him win today, too!

00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:44.480
The fifth round has finally started!

00:23:44.480 --> 00:23:46.770
The opponent is Bijoudai Sayama High.

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:53.360
Fourth batter Tajima has also recovered from his injury and faces the game in top shape.

00:23:53.360 --> 00:23:55.120
Mihashi also seems to be in good condition,

00:23:55.370 --> 00:24:00.200
and if we can win this game, we'll finally be in the best eight!

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:03.960
I'll also cheer with all my strength from the bench!

00:24:03.960 --> 00:24:04.830
Next time:

00:24:04.830 --> 00:24:06.000
Fifth Round.

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:09.130
That group of nine are very close, aren't they?
